  "lineage": "Formed in Léopoldville-Kinshasa and Brazzaville in the late 1940s-50s when Cuban son septet 78s on the GV series were re-heard through Kikongo and Lingala song, codified by Joseph Kabasele's African Jazz and Franco's OK Jazz on Ngoma, Loningisa and Surboum labels: moderate 4/4 clave-derived rhythm at roughly 100-125 BPM, interlocking clean single-coil guitars over walking electric bass, snare-and-hi-hat maracas-driven kit, two- and three-part Lingala vocal harmony in a soft mid-register, and a horn section of trumpet and saxophone answering the sung couplets.",
